      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Embedding Provider**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on an embedding provider. Based on popularity and general availability, I'm leaning towards Google Cloud's Vertex AI. The next step is to make this choice explicit within the `embed_batch.py` script.\n\n\n**Defining the embedding script**\n\nNow that I've selected Vertex AI, the `embed_batch.py` script needs to take shape. I'll utilize the `google.cloud.aiplatform` library. I'm planning a function called `embed_batch`, taking text input and returning embeddings. Imports and client initialization will also be included, making sure that Vertex AI is explicitly identified as the provider.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865480624,
          "start": 1789865478592
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4bc9c0001cCV12E6GmC91jN",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4bc44d0010YeSz1X4Gr1ZYs",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b43bc0ffeKsZ5ma53kW5mlK",
      "time_created": 1789865478592,
      "time_updated": 1789865480625
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "ebQJMu5Dgh1VtQT1",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from typing import List\nfrom google.cloud import aiplatform\n\ndef embed_batch(texts: List[str], project_id: str, location: str) -> List[List[float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates embeddings for a batch of texts using Google Cloud Vertex AI.\n\n    Args:\n        texts: A list of text strings to embed.\n        project_id: Your Google Cloud project ID.\n        location: The Google Cloud region (e.g., \"us-central1\").\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of embedding vectors, where each vector is a list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    aiplatform.init(project=project_id, location=location)\n    model = aiplatform.gapic.PredictionServiceClient()\n    endpoint = f\"projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}/publishers/google/models/text-embedding-004\" # Using text-embedding-004 model\n\n    instances = [{\"content\": text} for text in texts]\n    parameters = {\"auto_truncate\": True} # Example parameter\n\n    response = model.predict(endpoint=endpoint, instances=instances, parameters=parameters)\n\n    embeddings = []\n    for prediction in response.predictions:\n        embeddings.append(list(prediction[\"embeddings\"]))\n    return embeddings\n",
            "filePath": "embed_batch.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
            "filepath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-cjfh68j2/embed_batch.py",
